<!-- MAINTENANCE & EXTENSIBILITY -->
<h2>7. Maintenance & Extensibility</h2>

<h3>Adding a New Watch Model</h3>
<p>Open <code>src/data/watchData.js</code> and append a new object to the <code>watches</code> array:</p>
<pre><code>{
  id: 13,
  name: "Chrono Heritage Gold",
  brand: "Alberto Originals",
  category: "luxury", // 'luxury' | 'vintage' | 'smart' | 'classic'
  price: 4850,
  image: "/luxury_watch.png",
  description: "Handcrafted 18k gold chronograph with open caseback.",
  features: [
    "Swiss Automatic Caliber AO-88",
    "48-Hour Power Reserve",
    "Alligator Leather Strap",
  ],
  specs: {
    caseDiameter: "41mm",
    dialColor: "Champagne Gold",
    movement: "Automatic Chronograph",
    crystal: "Double-AR Sapphire",
    waterResistance: "50m / 165ft",
  },
  badge: "Limited Edition",
  inStock: true,
}</code></pre>
<p>The new timepiece will automatically appear in the <strong>Collections Grid</strong>, <strong>Category Filter</strong>, and the <strong>Price List Table</strong> with zero additional code changes.</p>

